## 🎯 Your HCL Commerce Integration

### What You're Building

```
EDS Storefront (Adobe Commerce Boilerplate)
         ↓
    [User Actions]
    - Add product to cart from PDP
    - View mini-cart in header
    - View full cart page
         ↓
Adobe I/O Runtime (Integration Agent's APIs)
    - /api/hcl/cart/add      ← POST product + quantity
    - /api/hcl/cart          ← GET current cart state
    - /api/hcl/cart/remove   ← POST orderItemId to remove
         ↓
HCL Commerce Backend
    - Manages guest sessions (WCToken, WCTrustedToken)
    - Manages actual cart/order data
    - Validates inventory
    - Calculates pricing
```

### Key Features You'll Deliver

✅ **Add to Cart Integration**
- User clicks "Add to Cart" on Product Detail Page (PDP)
- System calls HCL API via Integration Agent
- Validates product exists and is in stock
- Creates HCL guest session
- Adds product to HCL cart
- Shows success/error feedback

✅ **Mini-Cart Display**
- Shows cart summary in header
- Displays item count, cart total
- Lists items in dropdown
- Updates in real-time
- Remove item functionality

✅ **Full Cart Page**
- Displays all items with details
- Shows pricing breakdown (subtotal, tax, shipping)
- Allows quantity updates
- Allows item removal
- Links to checkout

✅ **Error Handling**
- Out of stock products
- Product not found
- API errors
- Network timeouts
- User-friendly messaging

